SWEET WLAN gap report (patch 0137, USER ORDER 2026-10-27 "no more silent failures; errors must scream").
Why: the Wi-Fi path refuses, skips and degrades in about 35 places that print an ordinary "SWEET WLAN:" line, and sweet_wlan_stage3()'s result was discarded ((void)swl_stage3).
What: swl_gap(area, what, sev) in sweet_wlan_wr.h prints "WIFI GAP: <area> <what> x<count> [<sev>]" at count 1, 2, 4, 8 ..., the text carries no run values so the key is stable between runs;
swl_gap_summary() (every exit of sweet_wlan_init that touched the chip path) prints "WIFI GAPS: N distinct, M total" and every entry with its final count. Calls sit right before every "refused", "not read", "not touched", "skipped",
"not implemented", "STOP" printf of sweet_wlan.c and sweet_wlan_wr.h, plus the unconditional W15 gap (cfg 0x88 |= 0x300 is not implemented, 0133 header) and a gap when swl_stage3() returns an error.
No register access, no behaviour change: logging only. Severity strings are PROPOSALS (guess). tools/xrun_report.py collects the lines; docs/KNOWN-GAPS-WIFI.md (super repo) is the list NEW is judged against.

